#  _Article and photos by Tani Du Toi_

EASTER eggs turned into music shakers when Rhythm Culture hosted a kids’ dance, sing and drumming workshop at Palmwoods’ Girl Guides hut on April 15. The participants brought their home-made shakers to the fun workshop hosted by Nathaniel Combs. The best shakers won prizes. During the workshop, Nathaniel took the parents and kids on a fun journey to Africa. They had lots of laughs as they travelled to Africa on planes, trains, trucks and submarines and when they got there, they imitated their favourite African animals. Along the way, Nathaniel taught the troupe drumming, and dance techniques and plenty of African words.
